1: # esm-patient-procedures-app
2: 
3: A microfrontend for [OpenMRS 3](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org) that records, displays, and manages clinical procedures in the patient chart. It is part of the [openmrs-esm-patient-chart](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart) monorepo.
4: 
5: Jira: [O3-5077](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5077)
6: 
7: ---
8: 
9: ## Features
10: 
11: - **Procedure overview widget** — compact table in the patient summary that lists each procedure with its date, paginated according to the configured page size.
12: - **Procedures detailed summary** — full-page table that adds procedure type, body site, start/end timestamps, status, and inline notes. Rows are expandable to show additional detail without leaving the page.
13: - **Record & edit form** — a side-panel workspace for creating and updating procedures. Supports:
14:   - Fuzzy concept search for procedure name, body site, status, and duration unit — all driven by configurable concept UUIDs.
15:   - Exact start date/time or estimated start date (year + optional month) for procedures where the precise date is not known.
16:   - End date/time and duration with unit.
17:   - Procedure type selection from the OpenMRS procedure type registry.
18:   - Free-text notes.
19: - **Delete confirmation** — modal that voids a procedure record.
20: 
21: ---
22: 
23: ## Backend
24: 
25: This app requires the [openmrs-module-emrapi](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-emrapi) module, which exposes the `/ws/rest/v1/procedure` REST endpoints used for all CRUD operations.
26: 
27: ---
28: 
29: ## Running locally
30: 
31: From the monorepo root:
32: 
33: ```bash
34: yarn start --sources 'packages/esm-patient-procedures-app'
35: ```
36: 
37: ---
38: 
39: ## Configuration
40: 
41: The app is configured through the [OpenMRS config system](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/frontend-modules/loading-modules#module-configuration). All keys live under `@openmrs/esm-patient-procedures-app`.
42: 
43: | Key | Type | Default | Description |
44: |---|---|---|---|
45: | `overviewPageSize` | Number | `5` | Rows per page in the procedures overview widget. |
46: | `detailedViewPageSize` | Number | `10` | Rows per page in the procedures detailed summary view. |
47: | `procedureConceptUuid` | UUID | `8d490bf4-…` | Scopes the procedure concept search. |
48: | `procedureConceptSourceType` | String | `Concept class` | How `procedureConceptUuid` filters results: `Concept class`, `Concept set`, `Answer to`, or `any`. |
49: | `bodySiteConceptUuid` | UUID | `8d491c7a-…` (Anatomy) | Scopes the body-site concept search. |
50: | `bodySiteConceptSourceType` | String | `Concept class` | Same options as above. |
51: | `statusConceptUuid` | UUID | `167157AAAA…` | Scopes the status concept search. |
52: | `statusConceptSourceType` | String | `Concept set` | Same options as above. |
53: | `durationUnitConceptUuid` | UUID | `1732AAAAA…` | Scopes the duration-unit concept search. |
54: | `durationUnitConceptSourceType` | String | `Answer to` | Same options as above. |
55: 
56: ---
57: 
58: ## Form fields
59: 
60: | Field | Required | Notes |
61: |---|---|---|
62: | Procedure | Yes | Fuzzy concept search |
63: | Procedure type | Yes | Dropdown from `/ws/rest/v1/proceduretype` |
64: | Body site | Yes | Fuzzy concept search |
65: | Start date known? | — | Toggle between exact datetime and estimated date |
66: | Start date/time | Yes (if date is known) | Full date + time picker |
67: | Estimated start date | Yes (if date is unknown) | Year required, month optional |
68: | End date/time | No | Must be on or after start date |
69: | Duration | No | Positive integer; requires a unit when set |
70: | Duration unit | Conditional | Required when duration is provided |
71: | Status | Yes | Concept search |
72: | Notes | No | Free text |
73: 
74: ---
75: 
76: ## Estimated start date
77: 
78: When the exact start date of a procedure is not known — common for historical procedures — clinicians can switch the start date toggle to **No** and enter a year (required) and month (optional). The stored value is an ISO partial date string (`YYYY` or `YYYY-MM`). In the UI, estimated dates are shown with a trailing `*` to distinguish them from precise timestamps.
79: 
80: ---
81: 
82: ## Related
83: 
84: - Ticket: [O3-5077](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5077)
85: - Requirements: [Procedure History — Confluence](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/projects/pages/589267006/Procedure+History)
86: - Architecture discussion: [OpenMRS Talk](https://talk.openmrs.org/t/procedures-app-architecture-questions/47948/19)
87: - Backend module: [openmrs-module-emrapi](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-emrapi/)
